# Supabase is optional. Without these, Moodbite still runs: preferences live in
# localStorage, there are no accounts, and nothing else changes.
#
# Both values are safe to expose to the browser. The anon key is protected by
# row level security, which 0001_profiles.sql sets up so a row is only ever
# readable by the user it belongs to.
#
# Project Settings -> API, in the Supabase dashboard.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://bvykfeqbwzxztuhnkhtj.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google Places, for "who does this well near me". Optional in the same way:
# without it that one button does not render and nothing else changes.
#
# SERVER ONLY. There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix on this and there must never be
# one: a Places key in the browser bundle gets scraped and billed to you. It is
# also the salt used to hash client IPs for the per-client daily cap, so it
# never leaves the server for two reasons rather than one.
#
# Restrict the key in the Cloud console before using it:
#   - API restriction  -> Places API (New), nothing else
#   - Quotas           -> a hard daily ceiling, plus a billing budget alert
# Application restrictions cannot help here: the call is made server side, and
# Vercel has no fixed IP to allow-list. The quota is the real protection.
#
# Asking for ratings puts the call in Google's Enterprise tier: 1,000 free a
# month, then about $35 per 1,000. The cap in 0009_places_quota.sql is set to
# 900, so the default configuration cannot produce a bill.
GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=
